even if that isn't the case, Forsaken is a game where small actions are always changing the ecology and therefore creating plot points. Think about how changing one thing will change at least three other things and you'll have story hooks for weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T17:57:53-08:00","id":1178624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178617#post1178617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you are right a snarky emoti is not enough, i have seen the deficient moderation of this forum. Mallus my man/woman you are a fanboy whose selfworth reside in this game being &quot;perfect&quot; when it isnt.<br /> <br /> You are sad, you are the kind of deficient fanboy that the moderation of this forum breed, the sick echo chamber that make a opp a shadow of it former self.<br /> <br /> So as good bye <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> you are awesome to discuss hope to see you in a better forum and mallus you are a fanboy. And RichT you are a unprofessional for letting that madman brucatto ruin M20!<br /> <br /> Bye bitches</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">And that folks is how you get a permaban. Can't say you weren't warned.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T19:06:58-08:00","id":1178645,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Will to Kill is Shared</u></b><br /> <br /> Kuruth, arguably the scariest thing personally for a werewolf, is something that starts in the players hands, because of course that killing instinct is something a player should willfully engage-but don't be afraid to pull it out yourself. You don't have to full on push out Kuruth, but that killing instinct is something you are allowed to underline statements with and drop in as a backlight. It is very much your tool, and you should always be ready to keep the character on edge by reminding them that the will to murder is a thing that is not firmly in their hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T19:29:12-08:00","id":1178648,"title":"","content":"I've ran one game of 1e forsaken (it was a short-lived one at that) and i've never had the chance to play in one. So this isnt exactly the voice of experience talking here.<br /> When 2e came out with its renewed focus on the hunt i was entranced with the idea of unconventional hunts. <br /> Instead of learning about, finding and killing gribblies, you could have a hunt for a zoning permit that is menacing the bar that the pack uses as a headquarter for example. I'm honestly not sure how that would run in practice (or even if it would be fun) but its something i've been really curious to try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T20:52:09-08:00","id":1178662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178648#post1178648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of learning about, finding and killing gribblies, you could have a hunt for a zoning permit that is menacing the bar that the pack uses as a headquarter for example. I'm honestly not sure how that would run in practice (or even if it would be fun) but its something i've been really curious to try.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of a trend in some comedies. Big mean developer or other authority figure attempts to screw the protagonists and they have to jump through hoops to get conventional things done in unconventional ways.<br /> <br /> You have similar off-beat hunts in things like heist movies (it's easy to imagine a polar opposite to the Lodge of the Shield dedicated to grand crimes) or adventures like the Indiana Jones or National Treasure series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:45:26-08:00","id":1178673,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice so far.<br /> <br /> One of the main things I was wondering about it how much variety in antagonists/prey can I have in the game. The book only really talks about werewolves, humans and spirits as prey. My game will take place in the dark ages and I will have some mythological cryptids as antagonists. So I am kind of wondering how often spirits need to be the focus of an adventure for the players to get the most out of their character's abilities and how often they can go after other things.<br /> <br /> Also, other than protectorates it doesn't look like WtF has anything equivalent to the mage Consilium. I have all the 1st edition books on pdf, and I have Packs, do any of them go into more high level werewolf politics? Obviously I haven't read much outside of the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 01-24-2018, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T22:20:03-08:00","id":1178683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178673#post1178673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the main things I was wondering about it how much variety in antagonists/prey can I have in the game. The book only really talks about werewolves, humans and spirits as prey. My game will take place in the dark ages and I will have some mythological cryptids as antagonists. So I am kind of wondering how often spirits need to be the focus of an adventure for the players to get the most out of their character's abilities and how often they can go after other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also hosts, claimed and idigam. Not counting things from other game lines which are always viable prey, or stranger monsters (in the back of the Predators book there's a few neat ones). Hosts are detailed best in Predators but they go into it elsewhere. Claimed have rules all over the place but are probably the easiest to really make as a monster, as spirits corrupting flesh and getting weird powers are all over the place, even fitting in for giants as they (especially Hive Claimed, those claimed by multiple spirits) tend to grow in size. So you could have a spirit of storms claim a person and get a lightning bolt hurling titan, or a spirit of nature could claim someone and give you a dryad or something like Poison Ivy. It could just be a matter of them being ridden, with a spirit not fully entering a person but hanging onto them, urging them to do things and feeding off of the Essence generated.<br /> <br /> Spirits are obviously a big part of the game, with each pack having a totem and getting their various Gifts from spirits and Renown from lunes (moon spirits). But they don't have to be primary antagonists. Each tribe is built to focus on killing one prey or another, and only the Bone Shadows focus on spirits (though they can hunt other things).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, other than protectorates it doesn't look like WtF has anything equivalent to the mage Consilium. I have all the 1st edition books on pdf, and I have Packs, do any of them go into more high level werewolf politics? Obviously I haven't read much outside of the core book. </div> </div> </div>That would mostly be in the protectorate, which can be pretty involved but unique to the experience. If you have access to Dark Eras, there's an interesting one in Forsaken by Rome, as the Iron Masters and Ivory Claws teamed up to essentially make the Roman Empire. But you have more immediate things like the one in Bristol in the core book. The Rage, a first edition book, goes into some detail about them though they call them clutches. And obviously the Pack book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-24-2018, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T23:18:47-08:00","id":1178690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178487#post1178487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere is the Darwinian nightmare of the Shadow more evident than with the pack's totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t understand what you mean by this part. Can you expand on it a little?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:14:10-08:00","id":1178752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178690#post1178690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t understand what you mean by this part. Can you expand on it a little?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to know this too. Frankly I'm not stoked about this whole darwinian nightmare take on spirits and the shadow. It doesn't seem to lend itself to having much diversity or nuance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:42:21-08:00","id":1178761,"title":"","content":"Is worse at the low levels when they are literally preying on each other, like animals. As you go up the pole it becomes more like feudal relationships were powerful spirits exact tithes of essence from their vassals and then sends it up the pole to its supperiors in turn, all up to the Gods of the Shadow at the very top. So animal on the low, weird politics above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:55:59-08:00","id":1178788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178761#post1178761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is worse at the low levels when they are literally preying on each other, like animals. As you go up the pole it becomes more like feudal relationships were powerful spirits exact tithes of essence from their vassals and then sends it up the pole to its supperiors in turn, all up to the Gods of the Shadow at the very top. So animal on the low, weird politics above.</div> </div> </div> </div>This the way I have understood the Shadow, like a dark Miyazaki inspired spirit world, but when people start talking about darwinian nightmare it makes me think that they think the Shadow is akin to some kind of Xenomorph killing ground, which isn't as interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:18:09-08:00","id":1178800,"title":"","content":"It depends, if you only ever interact with Rank 1-2 spirits that would the impression you would get, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:40:29-08:00","id":1178810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178752#post1178752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to know this too. Frankly I'm not stoked about this whole darwinian nightmare take on spirits and the shadow. It doesn't seem to lend itself to having much diversity or nuance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that even such a dreary approach allows for a staggering diversity. Note that the entire Earth's ecosystem has developed through Darwinian processes, and yet resulted in all kinds of adaptations. Consider this as a starting point:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecological_relationship\" target=\"_blank\">Ecological relationships</a><br /> <br /> Now imagine Eater-of-Carrion cooperating with Death-through-Roadkill. One has the form of a vulture, and uses its flight and keen eye to find prey. The other has the form of a truck, and slaughters their target with its speed and mass. Afterwards, they eat.<br /> <br /> Grasping-Seed, a burdock spirit, travels around by attaching parts of itself to passing Spirits. Like its physical counterpart - it doesn't harm them. Unlike its physical counterpart - it actually warns them of danger, so it can be carried farther.<br /> <br /> A canny visitor may insert themselves into a relationship like that, with no loss to themselves. That is because unlike most animals, Spirits can be negotiated with. Moreover, all these Spirits will appreciate having their portfolio strengthened in the Flesh, like through leaving food on the highway, or sowing burdock where it won't be razed. If you convince them your word is good, they will easily allow what's more beneficial to them. Although Spirits have to eat, not all Spirits have to eat you specifically, which gives you room to maneuver. Also remember to know your worth. A Spirit will take you out to dry if it can, but it will settle for a fair exchange if you can assert yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 01-24-2018, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:37:36-08:00","id":1178832,"title":"","content":"I figured that's where Malus was going with his reference to the totem. A spirit who on its own might end up as nothing, instead siding with what many spirits see as their enemy. And profiting from it. Their future strength is gained from outside of the natural order, and they basically get a free ride to break one of the big taboo of spirits, not crossing the Gauntlet, with the help of the same folks who often enforce that rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-24-2018, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:46:50-08:00","id":1178837,"title":"","content":"Another question I thought of. If human lives create resonance, do ghosts do the same thing. Will the ghost of a grieving lover that haunts a house attract spirits of grief to the house?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:50:47-08:00","id":1178841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178810#post1178810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that even such a dreary approach allows for a staggering diversity. Note that the entire Earth's ecosystem has developed through Darwinian processes, and yet resulted in all kinds of adaptations. Consider this as a starting point:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecological_relationship&amp;quot;]Ecological</a> relationships[/URL]<br /> <br /> Now imagine Eater-of-Carrion cooperating with Death-through-Roadkill. One has the form of a vulture, and uses its flight and keen eye to find prey. The other has the form of a truck, and slaughters their target with its speed and mass. Afterwards, they eat.<br /> <br /> Grasping-Seed, a burdock spirit, travels around by attaching parts of itself to passing Spirits. Like its physical counterpart - it doesn't harm them. Unlike its physical counterpart - it actually warns them of danger, so it can be carried farther.<br /> <br /> A canny visitor may insert themselves into a relationship like that, with no loss to themselves. That is because unlike most animals, Spirits can be negotiated with. Moreover, all these Spirits will appreciate having their portfolio strengthened in the Flesh, like through leaving food on the highway, or sowing burdock where it won't be razed. If you convince them your word is good, they will easily allow what's more beneficial to them. Although Spirits have to eat, not all Spirits have to eat you specifically, which gives you room to maneuver. Also remember to know your worth. A Spirit will take you out to dry if it can, but it will settle for a fair exchange if you can assert yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that IS pretty interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:58:44-08:00","id":1178845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1178837#post1178837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question I thought of. If human lives create resonance, do ghosts do the same thing. Will the ghost of a grieving lover that haunts a house attract spirits of grief to the house?</div> </div> </div> </div>The quick reply is &quot;if that makes for a good story, yes&quot;<br /> <br /> Otherwise the books tend to consider ghosts to be less impactful on the Shadow than the living ones. Humans are &quot;closer&quot; to the Shadow than ghosts when it comes to influence. I tend to look at it this way: to the eyes of spirits, the living are colored while the of the dead are black &amp; white. They might still be able to see them, but it does not have the same effect.<br /> <br /> Now, the impact ghosts have on the living does resonate as usual in the Shadow, so an infamous haunted house might attract spirit of fear, curiosity and death, meaning there's easily room to play with ghost and spiritis interacting with each other.<br /> <br /> Real trouble begins with those spirits who mess (or eat) ghosts or the circumstances that fuse the two together. Usually, that's when some really nasty creatures appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T12:19:55-08:00","id":1178896,"title":"","content":"<b>2E Advise: Remember there are Wolf-Blooded in game</b>. They were in 1E, but in 2E they were made wholly into useful subrace, with each member having few Tells - typical werewolves powers like changing into particular Form, talking to spirits, wolves fur instead of wounds or seeing ANY ephemeral being. They are not only cool by this - having some powers even Uratha do not have - they are even USEFUL in packs. More to it - you can ask starting players if they do not want to start playing WB instead of Uratha - to ease oneself before this whole 20+ pages of inner powers for 'proper' werewolves. \ud83d\ude0e There is even First Change scenario in 2E corebook in Storytelling chapter about changing from suddenly WB to full Uratha in very bloody night under the Moon... \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> And I made just simple game hack that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1095950-2e-hack-sacred-hunt-for-everyone\">gives each WB ability to perform their Tribes Sacred Hunt Rite</a> - so WB can send his Uratha brothers on his Tribe's Prey. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-25-2018, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:26:39-08:00","id":1179074,"title":"","content":"So I am a little confused by totem creation. I get you total up the total dots in the Totem merit that the pack has and use that to stat out the Totem. But what I don't see is how much do those stats cost? Is it a one for one trade, like one dot of the Totem merit is exchanged for 1 attribute point, 1 essence point, 1 numina, 1 gift or 1 influence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:55:09-08:00","id":1179086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1179074#post1179074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am a little confused by totem creation. I get you total up the total dots in the Totem merit that the pack has and use that to stat out the Totem. But what I don't see is how much do those stats cost? Is it a one for one trade, like one dot of the Totem merit is exchanged for 1 attribute point, 1 essence point, 1 numina, 1 gift or 1 influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>See Step Five of Creating the Totem, on page 92.<br /> <br /> Each Totem dot translates to an Attribute dot, and the total Attribute dots determine what the totem's Rank is. Each Totem dot <i>also</i> contributes to the totem's Essence capacity and number of Numina, without diverting any of those points from the totem's Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T21:45:39-08:00","id":1179105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1179086#post1179086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See Step Five of Creating the Totem, on page 92.<br /> <br /> Each Totem dot translates to an Attribute dot, and the total Attribute dots determine what the totem's Rank is. Each Totem dot <i>also</i> contributes to the totem's Essence capacity and number of Numina, without diverting any of those points from the totem's Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm blind as a bat. It is right there in step five. thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T21:49:30-08:00","id":1179107,"title":"","content":"Like Satchel says. Each Totem Merit is an Attribute dot. Totems have three Attributes: Power, Finesse, and Resistance. I believe you're supposed to start with 0, but it's easier to start with 1 each, like a PC. Each werewolf automatically has 1 Totem Merit, so if you have a group of players 5, you end up having 8 Attribute dots across the totem, still keeping it at Rank 1 (on p183, you can see Rank 1 ephemerals have 5-8 Attributes).<br /> <br /> It would have 2 Numen (p92, 'The spirit starts with one Numen. Every four Totem points grants the spirit an additional Numen.'), maximum Essence of 8 (lower of Totem points or maximum Essence), and has 1 Influence (p186, 'Spirits begin with dots in Influence equal to their Rank). They can trade out Numina for more Influences. They don't have Gifts. This spirit would be pretty weak but it would just take 1 Totem Merit to bring it to Rank 2, giving it another Influence. There's a bunch of derived traits on p185, like its Willpower is its Resistance+Finesse. Size you can just pick something appropriate for it, 5 is human-sized.<br /> <br /> The Pack book has rules for Pack Experience, which let the totem get its own Experience and spend that to get more Attributes, Influence, and Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T07:04:42-08:00","id":1179179,"title":"","content":"Are there any good resources for ban and bane ideas? I see a few threads about it, but wondering what everyone's favorite sources are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T08:38:22-08:00","id":1179213,"title":"","content":"I find the Predators book really good. The first chapter has a bunch of pre-made spirits, ranging from animal and elemental spirits to artificial and conceptual ones. They tend to offer loose descriptions, with the ban section being more about what kind of bans these spirits tend to have, rather than a specific one.<br /> <br /> For example, 'As transportation-spirits, train-spirits are frequently under ban to not remain in one area for more than a certain length of time. Others may be forbidden from accepting passengers, unable to travel in certain areas or conditions or unable to carry certain types of cargo.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T11:21:39-08:00","id":1179265,"title":"","content":"Totally agree with the praise for Predators. That book was a blessing. Book Of Spirits technically is not a Werewolf book but a general one, but still a solid resource overall.<br /> <br /> Between the two, though? Predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T14:21:01-08:00","id":1179311,"title":"","content":"Looking through it, it definitely has a lot of great ideas for bans, but a search of the PDF shows nothing about banes. We're banes not a thing in first edition? I can't remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T14:26:38-08:00","id":1179312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1179311#post1179311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking through it, it definitely has a lot of great ideas for bans, but a search of the PDF shows nothing about banes. We're banes not a thing in first edition? I can't remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banes and bans were sort of the same thing in first edition, all listed as bans. They were divided up in second so everything gets one of each. I don't believe there's a list anywhere to pull from, though there are some guided examples in the Ban and Bane section for making spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T00:56:41-08:00","id":1179457,"title":"","content":"We have also shared <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1174539-2e-your-totems\">fan created Totems topic</a>, with shown Bans and Banes of those spirits in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T01:46:58-08:00","id":1179462,"title":"","content":"Also try <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\">this homebrew content thread</a> by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T09:24:51-08:00","id":1179855,"title":"","content":"You should read some APs first, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","user":"viskarenvisla","date":". 01-28-2018, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T19:52:11-08:00","id":1184992,"title":"","content":"So we had our character creation session today. The players decided on an spirit whose ban is that is must be fed secrets, a variation on ritual sacrifice. So my question is what should I set the frequency for this at? I am assuming that the more powerful the totem ends up being the more unique or powerful the secret should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T20:01:41-08:00","id":1184997,"title":"","content":"A week sounds fair, especially considering how easy werewolf abilities make secret-finding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T06:52:20-08:00","id":1185564,"title":"","content":"So now I am wondering how much personality a totem spirit has. How well can it communicate with the pack? Can it make demands and requests? Can it give the pack missions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":".  Stupid Android. 02-13-2018, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T08:46:52-08:00","id":1185596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1185564#post1185564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now I am wondering how much personality a totem spirit has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on its Rank. Remember 1-2 you're working with something that acts on instinct and is considered comparable to an animal or child by other spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How well can it communicate with the pack? Can it make demands and requests? Can it give the pack missions? </div> </div> </div>The lower Rank, the less complex ideas it would be able to communicate, or form. But its ability to actually communicate them would probably depend on if it had any powers. Generally it has to be there and talk, but it might have an ability that lets it send messages over distances, for instance a computer spirit could e-mail you, or a technology spirit could text.<br /> <br /> They <i>can </i>make demands and requests, or give missions. But the totem isn't the boss of the pack, so that might not go over well, especially if abused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T08:55:47-08:00","id":1185601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1185564#post1185564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now I am wondering how much personality a totem spirit has. How well can it communicate with the pack? Can it make demands and requests? Can it give the pack missions?</div> </div> </div> </div>My own game's totem, a vengeful ancestor spirit who had most of it's bloodline exterminated, hence it clinging to existence by sheer will to be avenged, was at rank 1 when the game began. After several acts of asymmetric warfare, with casualties in the dozens, and a locus keyed and dedicated to it's nature, it is now rank 3.<br /> <br /> It began as a bloodthirsty fucking thing, a mist-shrouded hound. As it's rank began to rise, it began to influence the pack (note the lack of caption in influence) to be more poetic on it's approach to violence. More refined, within the boundaries of it's ban, obviously.<br /> <br /> Now it may approach a new rank with a motivation to rebuild it's bloodline. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 02-13-2018, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T09:48:49-08:00","id":1185618,"title":"","content":"So how are packs expected to handle their totem. Do they bind it to a fetish and carry it around with them or do they keep it someplace safe or do they let it run free?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T09:53:27-08:00","id":1185622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1185618#post1185618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how are packs expected to handle their totem. Do they bind it to a fetish and carry it around with them or do they keep it someplace safe or do they let it run free?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually they let it run free, maybe hanging with individual members or lingering around the spiritual center of the territory or traveling from packmember to packmember and checking on them (especially useful in the case of human and wolf-blooded and other non-werewolf packmates), or a locus of appropriate Resonance. Some location-based totems might not be able to move far from their spot. But generally you would want something mobile that can help in a hunt.<br /> <br /> A lot's going to depend on the pack and what spirit they end up finding.<br /> <br /> The book <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/181760/The-Pack\" target=\"_blank\">the Pack</a> really gets into what it's like being a member of a pack, including the wolf-blooded, human, and totem's point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2018, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T10:09:27-08:00","id":1185631,"title":"","content":"A totem is part of a pack, thus it's within the peeking order, and seldom atop it when it is concerned with Forsaken. On the contrary, Pure totems are often cruel task masters for their packs, demanding gruesome, inhuman bans from them.<br /> <br /> Clearly, the more powerful the spirit becomes, the more deference it is owed. If you have a bunch of rank 1 Uratha with a rank 4 totem, it'll be dominating them pretty easily, but a normal totemic relationship goes hand in hand with the upgrading of the Uratha's own rank within the shadow. My character also is recognized as a rank 3 werewolf, puts him as the alpha in the pack in equal footing to influence the totem, and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> Stuffing your totem into a fetish would most likely invalidate the totemic bond. It's not something you do to a packmate. You're literally jailing a spirit for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T17:25:11-08:00","id":1185782,"title":"","content":"So the join or die aspect of Basu-Im only mentions it affecting packmates. So I assume that a werewolf from another pack in Basu-Im won't cause this effect to my pack, correct? So if said raging werewolf wanders into my pack's territory, my pack can go confront and contain it without immediately setting of a chain reaction, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T18:36:26-08:00","id":1185794,"title":"","content":"That would be correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:21:45-08:00","id":1185845,"title":"","content":"But enemy Hard Raging werewolf will probably do you mass damage - then YOU risk Death Rage, form massive wounds taken. And if you go - your pack risk Death Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:53:54-08:00","id":1185847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1185782#post1185782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the join or die aspect of Basu-Im only mentions it affecting packmates. So I assume that a werewolf from another pack in Basu-Im won't cause this effect to my pack, correct? So if said raging werewolf wanders into my pack's territory, my pack can go confront and contain it without immediately setting of a chain reaction, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two ways of reading it, and I\u2019m pretty sure we\u2019ve never defined which is more correct. (Which is why I presented two Pack Merits dealing with Kuruth - one for each interpretation.)<br /> <br /> You can run it that only your pack rages, which has its advantages and disadvantages, or you can run it that any Bass-im has everyone raging, which has its advantages and disadvantages. Whichever works for your table, just make sure you\u2019re consistent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:58:45-08:00","id":1185850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1185618#post1185618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how are packs expected to handle their totem. Do they bind it to a fetish and carry it around with them or do they keep it someplace safe or do they let it run free?</div> </div> </div> </div>Option 1 is a very good way of no longer having a totem, unless there\u2019s a good reason why it wants to be bound into a fetish. Totems tend to hang around their pack and its territory, but aren\u2019t strictly carried around as a captive or anything.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, there\u2019s a lot of incentive for both pack and totem to treat each other with various levels of respect and equality. Every pack is different, and some will be more or less dominant, but many (Forsaken) packs have a symbiotic relationship with their totem, which works best for everyone. (As Malus said, Pure totems tend to be more powerful and more inclined to exert their dominance over the pack, but even then every pack is different.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T20:26:20-08:00","id":1186168,"title":"","content":"Are there any guidelines on how frequent or common Loci should be? Also, as I understand it there is also just free floating essence in the Shadow. How common is that? How hard should it be for Uratha to find essence in the shadow that isn't from a Loci.<br /> <br /> Also, do werewolves have to use the Sacred Hunt rite to eat spirits? Can't they just go into the hisil pick up a 0 rank spirit and eat it for its essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T21:00:50-08:00","id":1186171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186168#post1186168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any guidelines on how frequent or common Loci should be? Also, as I understand it there is also just free floating essence in the Shadow. How common is that? How hard should it be for Uratha to find essence in the shadow that isn't from a Loci.</div> </div> </div> </div>No real guidelines, it's up to you, but Lore of the Forsaken has some good advice for how to handle them. The big point is that they're in demand, spiritually. Forsaken aren't the only ones who want them, and having claimed access to one generally means the pack has muscle, as they've likely driven off spirits or other entities from it. So you don't want them to be too common, or the players have no need to concern themselves with Essence. They're a nice goal for packs to go after and can often be a hub of activity for antagonists. Though obviously if you want to play down that angle you can just have them wherever and let them focus on other things.<br /> <br /> There is free-flowing Essence, which is how spirits get fed and how loci form, but it's not generally something werewolves can pick up. Special Gifts or fetishes might make exceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do werewolves have to use the Sacred Hunt rite to eat spirits? Can't they just go into the hisil pick up a 0 rank spirit and eat it for its essence? </div> </div> </div>Without the Sacred Hunt rite, you're just hitting them. It's what allows werewolves to get Essence from the hunt. You can still kill spirits otherwise, you just won't get Essence from them. You can eat other werewolves and humans for Essence, though.<br /> <br /> There's ancient IC reasons for this that come up in their legends and the Neolithic Dark Era, but effectively they were made for a world that no longer exists, and rites (like the Sacred Hunt) and other powers have allowed them to adapt to these others (our real world and the Shadow), while never really being a part of either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-15-2018, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T21:16:05-08:00","id":1186172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186168#post1186168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any guidelines on how frequent or common Loci should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Loci are formed in places where a lot of Essence manages to build up without getting siphoned off by spirits and other entities, which tends to mean they're confined to low-traffic sites of significant age and/or potent emotional moments. Quantity and quality say things about your setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, as I understand it there is also just free floating essence in the Shadow. How common is that? </div> </div> </div>It isn't. That's patches of resonance, which allow compatible spirits to derive Essence through proximity, and there's the weird foodstuffs that appear near loci.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do werewolves have to use the Sacred Hunt rite to eat spirits? Can't they just go into the hisil pick up a 0 rank spirit and eat it for its essence? </div> </div> </div>No, for much the same reason that they can't just go down to the butcher shop and buy a pack of sausages to wolf down for Essence. There's certain notes you have to hit for that kind of predation to reinforce your nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T03:24:57-08:00","id":1186226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1185564#post1185564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now I am wondering how much personality a totem spirit has. How well can it communicate with the pack? Can it make demands and requests? Can it give the pack missions?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNot only can a totem make demands and requests, it absolutely should. Treat a totem as one of the most fully fleshed-out NPCs you use, as they're going to be interacting with the pack with regular frequency and can be a really useful driving force for a Storyteller to use. I've had my PC's pack totems demand they take out rival spirits to open vacancies in a court for the totem to move into, rebuild locations of importance to the spirit, gather seemingly bizarre collections of items as gifts for the totem, start sulking when they weren't treated by the PCs in the way they wanted to be treated, purposefully set PCs up to fail so that they can teach some symbolic lesson or just swoop in and save the day, throw tantrums, start favouring one particular pack member over the rest because that person most closely resonates with them (and has lots of Totem dots), dictate spirit-quests, pick fights with other spirit broods that the pack then gets dragged into, go on the spiritual equivalent of a drug bender, turn out not to be a spirit at all but rather a Purified pretending to be one, pitch philosophical conundrums to the pack to which the answers fundamentally change what the spirit is, evolve into a new form after the pack have done enough things for the totem, become so tightly bonded and loyal to the pack that the spirit actually sacrificed itself to save its pack in absolute defiance of the usual self-interested approach spirits take, have staring contests with pack members due to unfortunate misunderstandings, and manifest at decidedly unhelpful times in the home of a pack member who was trying to maintain a semblance of normalcy with their mundane human family.<br /> <br /> \u200bNothing requires a pack to act on demands, requests or passive-aggressive suggestions as to what they should do for the totem, but a pack that ignores their totems' drives and needs is likely to, at the very least, get a grumpy and uncooperative totem.<br /> <br /> \u200bCommunication varies depending on the spirit in question. I had a spirit of electrical power that always communicated with its pack via hijacking nearby electric devices and speaking through them, so half-way through the Rahu's favourite TV show the screen would garble and start speaking in creepy hissing static at him. Some spirits will act more aloof, expect the pack to regularly check in with them to find out if there's anything the totem needs, and sulk or get angry if the pack doesn't figure this out. Some spirits will be there, all the time, overeager, manifesting messages into the Flesh or outright appearing, possibly like very enthusiastic dogs that just won't leave a favoured pack mate alone. Some are balanced in their approach to communicating with the pack, in which case their weirdness is probably expressed in some other form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T03:55:36-08:00","id":1186230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186226#post1186226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... turn out not to be a spirit at all but rather a Purified pretending to be one...</div> </div> </div> </div>... Oh? And what might this delicious tidbit be? (Or is this already possible in Immortals?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b... Some spirits will act more aloof, expect the pack to regularly check in with them to find out if there's anything the totem needs, and sulk or get angry if the pack doesn't figure this out. ...... </div> </div> </div>And now I can't get out of my head the image of a totem acting like a slighted lover <i>saying </i>she's not angry, but <i>clearly </i>pouting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:44:49-08:00","id":1186304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186172#post1186172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loci are formed in places where a lot of Essence manages to build up without getting siphoned off by spirits and other entities, which tends to mean they're confined to low-traffic sites of significant age and/or potent emotional moments. Quantity and quality say things about your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume it might also be possible that a loci forms because a higher rank spirit shoos away lower spirits and purposely let's the essence accumulate. Whether that is because he is purposely trying to create a loci or just because he is a hoarder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:44:30-08:00","id":1186319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186304#post1186304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it might also be possible that a loci forms because a higher rank spirit shoos away lower spirits and purposely let's the essence accumulate. Whether that is because he is purposely trying to create a loci or just because he is a hoarder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, a werewolf might do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T10:03:39-08:00","id":1186346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186319#post1186319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely, a werewolf might do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I figured. If a Werewolf can do it, why not a higher rank spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T17:20:01-08:00","id":1186483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186346#post1186346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what I figured. If a Werewolf can do it, why not a higher rank spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these things happen, but the fact of the matter is that this is still, in practice, liable to result in loci being formed in defensible (or at least out-of-the-way) location due to the basic realities of maintaining a stockpile in a place where everything is hungry for that resource and conscious attention tends to directly correlate with new mouths to feed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:39:47-08:00","id":1186655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186483#post1186483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of these things happen, but the fact of the matter is that this is still, in practice, liable to result in loci being formed in defensible (or at least out-of-the-way) location</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as a place where people almost never go like a remote forest or an rural abandoned building maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:53:03-08:00","id":1186661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186655#post1186655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such as a place where people almost never go like a remote forest or an rural abandoned building maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a roof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T12:13:08-08:00","id":1186769,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Keep in mind werewolves do have more than a few ways to simply block off places, even without magic they can simply build a wall.<br /> <br /> A coordinated pack of decent (3-5) size could take turns watching over an area, doing active patrols in shifts, supplemented with Gifts of Warding and Pack Awareness and so forth in order to form a locus.<br /> <br /> Guaranteeing the right Essence was created might be the hard part but that's also doable.<br /> <br /> It just involves some work, and of course when it's done you have a valuable resource that might attempt to be taken. So one should stay on guard, but that's not particularly surprising. That may have been something Satchel was alluding to, the idea that a highly defensible stance may generate very defensive Essence and Locus, as opposed to some other desirable Resonance. There's always Resonance Shaping, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-16-2018, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:17:06-08:00","id":1186842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186769#post1186769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guaranteeing the right Essence was created might be the hard part but that's also doable.<br /> <br /> It just involves some work, and of course when it's done you have a valuable resource that might attempt to be taken. So one should stay on guard, but that's not particularly surprising. That may have been something Satchel was alluding to, the idea that a highly defensible stance may generate very defensive Essence and Locus, as opposed to some other desirable Resonance. There's always Resonance Shaping, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a werewolf is just trying refill his tank, does it matter what the resonance of the locus is?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:22:46-08:00","id":1186843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186769#post1186769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may have been something Satchel was alluding to, the idea that a highly defensible stance may generate very defensive Essence and Locus, as opposed to some other desirable Resonance. There's always Resonance Shaping, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly alluding to the fact that it's a lot easier to ward off grazers from a locus in a room at the end of a hallway than from a statue in the middle of a public park, but yes, cultivating a resonance that's suitable to being well-kept and attracting things that will behave themselves has narrative advantages as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:23:23-08:00","id":1186844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186842#post1186842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf is just trying refill his tank, does it matter what the resonance of the locus is?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Resonance doesn't matter for a werewolf if they're just getting Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:50:58-08:00","id":1186924,"title":"","content":"Is there a guide on how to determine if an opponent is an appropriate challenge for the players or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T22:32:25-08:00","id":1186945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1186924#post1186924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a guide on how to determine if an opponent is an appropriate challenge for the players or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem as far as I can tell is that two characters with, say, 100 Experiences each could go in entirely different ways, with one throwing it all into Combat and another spreading it out across Social and Mental Skills. For the most part you can deal with this by having access to the character sheets of PCs. If someone has, say, Tongue of Flame and 4 Purity, you know they can create fire, so a single antagonist whose bane is fire is probably not going to last long. Alternatively if the average Defense of the group is 2-3, an antagonist with a combat dicepool of 15 is likely going to be able to hit them pretty badly.<br /> <br /> Another aspect is the group. Some play with small or solo (one on one) games, some have groups with a lot of people (I believe someone was plotting one with 12 on the forum, though it wasn't playing with them all at the same time), some mix gamelines, skewing things even further. Generally if you have a single PC-like antagonist like a werewolf with 50 Experiences on top of what the werewolf PCs have, or just flat out better than the PCs, with 2 dots above every PC, they're still generally going to be confined to one action, compared to the group's however many. There's a little advantage for groups, too, in that every attack against a target that uses their Defense lowers it by 1 for further attackers in the turn, cumulatively, so an enemy with Defense 4 at the start of their turn could be working with Defense 0 by the end. You can deal with this, obviously, by having multiple enemies (werewolf packs, hosts and spirits do this well) though that can get clunky, or powerful enemies that require nonstandard means of combat (like an idigam).<br /> <br /> There's just a lot to factor in in determining that kind of thing. I think they should start publishing advice, there's not a lot on the story-building front for things, it usually tends towards variants of play rather than basic how-tos. Obviously it would be useful.<br /> <br /> That said, spirits and Claimed and hosts have been printed up in first edition books (as well as second edition's core) and don't require that much conversion to move them up to second edition rules. Werewolves are generally harder, but given the toolbox and storytelling nature of the game it's reasonable to make up powers beings might have gained through sacrifice or hard-to-find Gifts, though you usually want to at least play them consistently. There's also a fair amount of homebrew on the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T01:15:46-08:00","id":1186980,"title":"","content":"The way I've seen challenges taken in werewolf hasn't been binary outcomes of &quot;We did it! We hunted down the baddie!&quot;. Generally there's a price to pay in order to uphold the Hunt, be it in terms of personal relationships ruined against the risk of say, letting the Herd know, even to the detriment of said person's specific mental health.<br /> <br /> When you've reached the stage of &quot;we did it, we hunted down the baddie!&quot; it usually comes with several buts, such as &quot;but we lost two wolfblooded packmates, to it, but we went into Kuruth and wholesome slaughtered several innocents; but we had to infect people with yellow fever in order to exploit it's ban and bane, and now there's an epidemic&quot;. It's a damned if you do, damned if you don't world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T13:46:40-08:00","id":1191740,"title":"","content":"I assume werewolves are just as susceptible to drowning and poison as humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T14:08:22-08:00","id":1191743,"title":"","content":"Drowning doesn't have any rules, but all Uratha reduces the Toxicity of poisons and diseases by their Primal Urge dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T21:54:02-08:00","id":1191835,"title":"","content":"Re: Drowning<br /> <br /> You get a number of turns equal to stamina, past that you take 1 bashing damage per turn which you can't regenerate while still choking or drowning, once you reach unconsciousness it's just a matter of killing blow to destroy the windpipe or simply let time take it's course and completely fill you with aggravated damage, in environmental situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:38:24-08:00","id":1191922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1191835#post1191835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Drowning<br /> <br /> You get a number of turns equal to stamina, past that you take 1 bashing damage per turn which you can't regenerate while still choking or drowning, once you reach unconsciousness it's just a matter of killing blow to destroy the windpipe or simply let time take it's course and completely fill you with aggravated damage, in environmental situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that your houserule or an official ruling that was made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 03-05-2018, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:42:39-08:00","id":1191924,"title":"","content":"Those were the rules in first edition at least. And yeah, the rule was 1 minute per dot out of combat or 1 turn per dot while in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  clarification 03-05-2018, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:42:47-08:00","id":1191925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1191835#post1191835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Drowning<br /> <br /> You get a number of turns equal to stamina, past that you take 1 bashing damage per turn which you can't regenerate while still choking or drowning, once you reach unconsciousness it's just a matter of killing blow to destroy the windpipe or simply let time take it's course and completely fill you with aggravated damage, in environmental situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think a number of<i> minutes</i> equal to Stamina would be more appropriate (Unless in combat, in which case it becomes a number of turns). I know they had rules for this in 1e, and this sounds like them as far as I can remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T09:37:49-08:00","id":1191972,"title":"","content":"We had our second session last night and because the pack are Vikings that live on an island and are sailors, the idea was brought up that tossing someone who was death raging into the sea would be a good way to let them ride it out with minimal collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T09:57:21-08:00","id":1191979,"title":"","content":"Also this question came up yesterday. Can a Werewolf detect if something is being urged, possessed or claimed with their natural senses or does that require a gift, like Scent the Unnatural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T11:15:38-08:00","id":1191997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1191979#post1191979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also this question came up yesterday. Can a Werewolf detect if something is being urged, possessed or claimed with their natural senses or does that require a gift, like Scent the Unnatural?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just being urged, the spirit is likely around it. So you might just see if there's a spirit lurking forbodingly over a person.<br /> <br /> If they're Urged, Possessed or Claimed a Gift or the Storm Lord Sacred Hunt benefit could do it, too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T13:43:19-08:00","id":1192745,"title":"","content":"The rules say that werewolves can learn a shadow gift from a spirit as part of a Sacred Hunt. Is there a way for werewolves to determine which spirits know a gift or can they learn a gift from any spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:26:15-08:00","id":1192769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1192745#post1192745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules say that werewolves can learn a shadow gift from a spirit as part of a Sacred Hunt. Is there a way for werewolves to determine which spirits know a gift or can they learn a gift from any spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Cahalith and Ithaeur job to determine (by tales and lore recorded, or a network of spirits letting you know what one is capable of), with an Elodoth helping if you directly inquire to the spirit in question, but given how, to unlock gifts you just need a passing match of essence (IE, night spirits could impart evasion and/or stealth gifts, any elemental could impart the elemental gift to be unlocked in your character's essence) Further facet learning requires no further spiritual involvement save the attainment of more renown.<br /> <br /> My character has spirit contacts, which he consults whenever he'll seek a worthy prey on those grounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T22:53:14-07:00","id":1198969,"title":"","content":"So it verboten for Uratha to use silver, but what are the mores concerning non-Uratha pack members using silver weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T23:51:15-07:00","id":1198976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1198969#post1198969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it verboten for Uratha to use silver,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a breaking point towards the flesh, it doesn't seem to be forbidden, let alone by any authority. There's several mentions of it being used by Forsaken in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but what are the mores concerning non-Uratha pack members using silver weapons? </div> </div> </div>It pops up in one of the stories in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/138981/The-Idigam-Chronicle-Anthology\" target=\"_blank\">Idigam Chronicle Anthology</a>. There, it seems to be an 'It's fine if it helps him sleep better but if they start getting ideas we'll do something about it' point of view. It may seem like a nice idea, and give a pack member a morale boost, but if they use it against another werewolf they're more likely to push them into Kuruth than kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T07:02:13-07:00","id":1200415,"title":"","content":"So I ran my first full session this weekend. Is it just me or are Defense ratings overall too high?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T07:09:34-07:00","id":1200418,"title":"","content":"Do you have an example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:30:13-07:00","id":1200439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1200418#post1200418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. But it seems to be really easy to get a Defense of 5 or 6 with even a rank 2 or 3 spirit. Which is basically equal to the combat dice pools the players had.<br /> <br /> So the players found their dice pools regularly reduced to 1 or 2 dice without spending Willpower. Which they found frustrating when they are regularly missing their targets, which made combat drag on. They only made real progress by basically ganging up on every target. Having to use the same tactic over and over again to succeed doesn't make for very interesting combats. The game seems to mechanically favor defense over attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:46:36-07:00","id":1200448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1200439#post1200439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the players found their dice pools regularly reduced to 1 or 2 dice <b>without spending Willpower.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the whole idea \u2014 violent encounters are stressful to get through without being a drain on the average character's reserves of special effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T09:18:13-07:00","id":1200456,"title":"","content":"Yeah; in combat, werewolves in particular have a lot of ways to squeeze out additional dice. the +Str from the forms, the 1/scene free Tilts from Urshul that can really muck a target up, ganging up to get the multiple attackers Defence penalty, Willpower, and all-out attacks, are all ways to crank out the offence.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor example, a relatively basic starting werewolf with only a little effort spent on combat - let's say Strength 2, Brawl 1 - is looking at a base dice pool of 5 in Urshul, which goes up to 10 with a Willpower point and all-out attack to land a crippling Tilt on the victim. Gang up so that one or two other pack members have knocked off some of the target's Defence, and it may not even be necessary to go for the dice adders. Hit Gauru for even more Strength and the target doesn't get to add their Athletics (or other skill) to their basic Defence score. As soon as you move into an actual combat-specced character - let's say Str 3, Brawl 3 and a specialty, it gets trivial to reach for nearly 10 dice without any adders whatsoever, and that's not considering for ex. Gifts.<br /> <br /> \u200bMeanwhile, Rank 2 spirits are meaningful opponents, and Rank 3 you're starting to look at heavier-weight opponents. The Shadow is <i>dangerous</i>\u200b, and if the pack are going after Rank 3 spirits early on without having combat-specialised pack members, they can expect to be challenged and have trouble getting past that sort of Defence - they'll need to play smart, gang up, etc etc. to deal with it.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut a pack with even a moderate focus on combat abilities is probably going to find Def 5 or 6 a breeze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 03-28-2018, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T09:24:42-07:00","id":1200461,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Need some Athletics, it's the all-purpose Defense Attribute. Except for some superpowers.<br /> <br /> There's a couple nice Gifts and tactics that help deal with this, though, like Crushing Blow, which lowers a target's Defense by the striker's Honor for them and packmates, or the Flanking Merit.<br /> <br /> In our last game while one werewolf dueled another, another ended up fighting a pair of wolf-blooded martial artists. They had really big Defense compared to the werewolf (I believe it was 6 to her 4) but Willpower, Tilts, getting rid of their weapons so they were only doing Bashing, and knocking them into wound penalties got rid of them pretty easily.<br /> <br /> But like Acrozatarim said, Rank 3 opponents are like an equivalent of special human or low-ranked supernatural. In D&amp;D it might be like low level but classed ogre. Compared to Rank 2's classed orcs (easier to deal with en masse but still dangerous).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-28-2018, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T10:56:45-07:00","id":1200486,"title":"","content":"Okay, well it sounds like we are doing things mostly right. Most of the players speced for social, intrigue and magic, not combat. So I just need to get a handle on what an appropriate combat encounter for them is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T11:06:40-07:00","id":1200489,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing because you mentioned the 'gang up' thing you know that whenever a character uses their Defense in a turn (like they're being attacked) their Defense is lowered by 1 the next time they're attacked in a turn. So depending on initiative the last werewolf will generally deal with a lower Defense. It also really makes groups dangerous, giving a benefit to even untrained combatants (and werewolves with powerful natural Lethal weapons and higher Strength really turn that slight benefit to a big one).<br /> <br /> I just mention it because it's something some people have missed before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-28-2018, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T12:54:28-07:00","id":1200529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1200489#post1200489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing because you mentioned the 'gang up' thing you know that whenever a character uses their Defense in a turn (like they're being attacked) their Defense is lowered by 1 the next time they're attacked in a turn. So depending on initiative the last werewolf will generally deal with a lower Defense. It also really makes groups dangerous, giving a benefit to even untrained combatants (and werewolves with powerful natural Lethal weapons and higher Strength really turn that slight benefit to a big one).<br /> <br /> I just mention it because it's something some people have missed before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we we're aware of that rule, that was how they we're able to finally defeat their opponents by deciding to concentrate their attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T13:52:30-07:00","id":1200555,"title":"","content":"Sounds like everything went as it should, then. Good for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T12:48:21-07:00","id":1233484,"title":"","content":"Now that i have about a half a dozen sessions under my belt I thought i would come back to this thread and put my own advice to new Storytellers in here.<br /> <br /> Out of the box Werewoles are already near indestructable. This is especially true if they still have essence or willpower left or still have the option to voluntarily go into War form. Because of that you dont have to worry much about TPKs and have a lot of leeway in designing antagonists. I fretted at first over designing a balanced encounter, still in D&amp;D mode thinking, but found that encounters I thought might be too challanging weren't or the characters were able to easily bounce back from defeats.<br /> <br /> Wilpower is a very important resource early on. My players had trouble managing it at first. Then we realized that making sure your pack member's blood and bone synergized is pretty important. For example, if everyone takes Guru they are going to have a hard time getting back willpower but if for every Guru there is a Cub then wilpower will flow a lot better.<br /> <br /> The first two sessions my players had issues gaining beats. Second Edition places a lot of the responsibility for gaining XP on players actions. So you may need to emphasize to your players on how they can get beats. The easiest way to gain beats is through gaining and resolving conditions. The two easiest ways the players have to gain conditions is the Sacred Hunt and the less well known flairing renown. They should be doing these every session. Also every session, when possible, they should be taking a voluntary dramatic failure. This gives the player an immediate beat and since most dramatic failures also lead to gaining a condition they can potentilly gain 2 beats from a single dramatic failure. Also make sure at least one of their character`s asperations is something that can be easily accomplished each session, such as &quot;start a fight&quot; or negotiate with a spirit&quot;. If the players are doing these they should be getting about 5 beats a session.<br /> <br /> i have more i might post later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T04:02:23-07:00","id":1233648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1233484#post1233484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first two sessions my players had issues gaining beats. Second Edition places a lot of the responsibility for gaining XP on players actions. So you may need to emphasize to your players on how they can get beats. The easiest way to gain beats is through gaining and resolving conditions. The two easiest ways the players have to gain conditions is the Sacred Hunt and the less well known flairing renown. They should be doing these every session. Also every session, when possible, they should be taking a voluntary dramatic failure. This gives the player an immediate beat and since most dramatic failures also lead to gaining a condition they can potentilly gain 2 beats from a single dramatic failure. Also make sure at least one of their character`s asperations is something that can be easily accomplished each session, such as &quot;start a fight&quot; or negotiate with a spirit&quot;. If the players are doing these they should be getting about 5 beats a session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus one for finishing the session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T08:25:06-07:00","id":1233711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1178431-your-advice-for-a-new-wtf-2e-storyteller?p=1233648#post1233648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus one for finishing the session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes that is something that will occur regardless of what the players do. I was pointing out that these specific beats require player agency to be gained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}